{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553350-making-sense-of-boar-as-a-garou-totem","id":1553350,"title":"Making Sense of Boar as a Garou Totem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-21T15:25:11-07:00","id":1553350,"title":"Making Sense of Boar as a Garou Totem","content":"So Boar has long b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bn a Tot<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bm option for Garou, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bv<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bn app<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200baring in multipl<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b cor<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b rul<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bbooks. But has any att<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bmpt <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bv<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200br b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bn mad<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b to <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200bxplain why Boar would hav<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b anything to do with th<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b Garou aft<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">er the</span></span>\u200by kill off th<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b Grondr in th<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b War of Rag<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">e</span></span>\u200b?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T15:36:03-07:00","id":1553352,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's ever been an official attempt to deal with it (which is the norm... there's a lot of Totems over the years that you'd expect to not like the Garou because of the Wars of Rage that don't seem to care, and even if it is addressed it's not always a negative). For the most part, it doesn't seem like the Incarna hold a major grudge about this; which makes sense since denying active followers is not really in their interest.<br /> <br /> It's worth remembering that the Grondr as we think of them now weren't canonically even a thing for most of WtA's history. The first book to actually imply that they were extinct fera killed by the Garou was the Mokole book from 1999. Before that what exactly was the connection of these pig people that were corrupted into the Skullpigs was very nebulous in the books. So a big reason is probably because Boar was in three core books before WtA Revised officially canonized the Grondr as we now think of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T15:49:13-07:00","id":1553354,"title":"","content":"We also have to keep in mind that, while their thematic connection is obvious, the totems of the Fera aren't necessarily all that intertwined with the respective Fera.<br /> <br /> They are not their creators, nor were their ascension as spirits linked to their Fera, as far as we know. While some, like Bat, may imply otherwise, they're actually the unexplained ones in the setting.<br /> <br /> So the game sometimes makes this a huge deal, sometimes not, but neither was ever actually explained on why it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T18:14:12-07:00","id":1553357,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember that the Grondr did not exist in the original setting. No mention of them is made in the Werewolf Player's Guide, first edition which introduced the Changing Breeds. The War of Rage is mentioned, but no mention of any Changing Breeds actually completely destroyed. So there is no problem for Boar being a Garou totem in 1e/2e because of lore associated with the Grondr's extinction.<br /> <br /> The Grondr are first mentioned (I believe, I could be wrong) in 1999's Mokole sourcebook in very, very late 2e era which makes it part of the Revised era in my opinion because the Revised metaplot changes of Vampire were already in effect. At that point the retcons keep coming. The Skull Pigs, originally described as a monster found only in the New World as a result of Wyrm minions corrupting javelinas, suddenly become linked to the Grondr. The Revised authors never saw fit to explain why Boar did not have any problems with the Garou leaving it to the STs to figure out. In many ways, the Revised setting is a completely different setting than 1e/2e although utilizing the same concepts in much the same way DC Comics had an Earth-One and Earth-Two that had characters of the same name, but being respectively their Silver Age and Golden Age versions.<br /> <br /> If it was important to me that the Grondr to have once existed in my setting and to explain why Boar has no issues with the Garou, I would use my standard explanation in my setting for the War of Rage. Which is that the &quot;War of Rage&quot; is a historians' construction much like the Hundred Years War is IRL. It is Galliards making up a narrative way after the fact, but without the benefit of actual historical resources but lots of local legends and mythology. The &quot;War of Rage&quot; as described in the books never really happened. Instead you have lots of different, non-related events included with a artistic (not historical) epic poetry narrative promoting whatever the values are for that specific era.<br /> <br /> Originally most Garou did not see anything bad about the &quot;War of Rage&quot; and used it as proof that the other Fera were assholes. However, by the late twentieth century a general feeling that the other Fera are needed to save Gaia makes Garou more sympathetic to them, and Children of Gaia guilt mongering blamed everything on the other tribes. The Fera, of course, took advantage of that to whitewash and ignore any of their crimes or mistakes they may have made thousands of years of ago. In truth, there was plenty of blame to go along. How does this come back to the Boar totem? Well, the Boar totem obviously doesn't feel the Garou are to be blamed (at least, not more than anything else). Which indicates there is probably more blame to go to one or more of the other Fera or perhaps some Wyrm minions in regards to the extinction of the Grondr. Your mileage on that explanation may be different.<br /> <br /> Because the Grondr are a retcon and their creators did not bother to think through the implications of it, I suggest you make any changes necessary to their backstory in order to make you feel comfortable with how the Boar totem is portrayed in your chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-22-2025, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T12:34:30-07:00","id":1553382,"title":"","content":"Well the most straightforward answer is that Boar, being a totem of War, regards the Grindr\u2019s defeat as fair combat and accept the outcome accordingly - especially if the relationship between this totem and Garou packs precedes the War of Rage, in which case there may have been battles fought between followers of Boar on both sides.<br /> <br /> The fact that the survivors of the Grondr went to the Wyrm rather than die fighting might also leave enough room for a rapprochement between the Totem and the Garou (Especially after millennia of chiminage).<br /> <br /> Doubtless there\u2019s a mighty tale at the root of it all, even if we don\u2019t yet know the verses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}